From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:31:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg: Leave SdhciNonPciDxe out of the payload

SdhciNonPciDxe registers the SDHCI controllers that coreboot leaves off
the PCI bus (the ACPI-mode SCC of Bay Trail and Braswell, the fixed MMIO
eMMC of AMD Picasso) from the LB_TAG_SDHCI_NONPCI record of the coreboot
table, for NonDiscoverablePciDeviceDxe to drive. No board of ouroBIOS
has such a controller, and no board of theirs writes the record: the
driver was dispatched at every boot to find nothing.

The module, its GUID and header, the record in Coreboot.h and the parser
of CbParseLib go, as before MrChromebox's commit 5342f428abac; so does
NonDiscoverablePciDeviceDxe, which only that driver fed and which
TianoCore's UefiPayloadPkg does not list. The SD block of the platform
is TianoCore's again: SdMmcPciHcDxe, EmmcDxe and SdDxe.
